        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3605585e-6052-5133-9dfd-427297e1a3b0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paola Suárez, Virginia Ruano Pascual, Michael Venus, Chan Hao-ching, Monica Niculescu\n- Topics: Tennis, doubles rankings, Grand Slam titles, Wimbledon, US Open\n\nFacts:\n- Paola Suárez was born on 23 June 1976 and is a retired professional tennis player from Argentina.\n- Michael Venus reached a career-high singles ranking of 274 in July 2011.\n- Paola Suárez was one of the most prominent women's doubles players of the early and mid-2000s.\n- Paola Suárez won eight Grand Slam titles in women's doubles, and all eight were won with Virginia Ruano Pascual.\n- Paola Suárez held the world No. 1 doubles ranking for 87 non-consecutive weeks.\n- In 2017, Chan Hao-ching reached the Wimbledon women's doubles final with Monica Niculescu.\n- In 2017, Chan Hao-ching reached the US Open mixed doubles final with Michael Venus.\n- Michael Venus is better known as a leading doubles player with a huge serve.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9220dd49-d5e6-57f8-97a0-eff07733f06b",
        "text": "Page: Paola Suárez. Sentence: Paola Suárez (born 23 June 1976) is a retired professional tennis player from Argentina.\nPage: Paola Suárez. Sentence: She was one of the most prominent women's doubles players throughout the early and mid-2000s, winning eight Grand Slam titles, all of them with Virginia Ruano Pascual, and holding the No. 1 doubles ranking for 87 non-consecutive weeks.\nPage: Michael Venus (tennis). Sentence: He reached a career high singles ranking of 274 in July 2011, but is much better known as a leading doubles player with a huge serve.\nPage: Chan Hao-ching. Sentence: She reached two more in 2017: the women's doubles at Wimbledon with Monica Niculescu, and the US Open mixed doubles with Michael Venus.",
